# Audited lock()/bust_lock()/force_bust_lock() call sites excluded from the
# lock-call gate.
#
# Format: file:line  # rationale
#   file:line is the repo-relative path and the line number of the lock() call
#   as reported by the grep scan.  A new lock() call added anywhere else in one
#   of these files is still caught by the gate.
#
# All 14 sites are on the child_process() dispatch path and are grandchild-
# unreachable (audited in 96e7cd26ef56 and 60b11ae678b5).
cmp_hints/field.c:185          # cmp_hints_field_record(): per-pool claim-and-insert on child dispatch path; grandchildren skip child_process() so this is unreachable from a grandchild
cmp_hints/pool.c:28            # pool_lock() helper wrapper; called only from cmp-hints routines on child_process() dispatch path; grandchild-unreachable
cmp_hints/pool.c:635           # shared_tier insert path called from child dispatch; lock held only for the linear-probe insert; no fork() on this call chain
cmp_hints/pool.c:948           # shared_tier read-sample path called from child dispatch; symmetric with the insert path above; no fork() on this call chain
random_syscall/chain-persist.c:191  # chain_corpus_persist(): snapshots ring under lock before unlocked disk write; called from child_process() persist path; no fork() on path
random_syscall/chain-persist.c:455  # chain_corpus_load(): ring slot write during corpus restore at startup/child init; no fork() between corpus load and this lock site
random_syscall/chain-corpus.c:237   # chain_corpus_save(): ring slot write on child dispatch; called from child_process() post-exec path; grandchild-unreachable
args/pools/blob_corpus.c:99    # blob_corpus_try_get_base(): lock around slot scan for buf fetch; called from child_process() arg-setup path; no fork() on this chain
args/pools/blob_corpus.c:178   # blob_corpus_promote_pending(): lock around pending-slot promotion after child dispatch; child_process() post-exec only; grandchild-unreachable
tables/table-activate.c:219    # deactivate_syscall_locked(): holds syscalltable_lock for deactivation; called only from child deactivation paths; no fork() on call chain
persist/minicorpus-core.c:102  # minicorpus_ring_lock() wrapper; called only from child_process() minicorpus persist path; grandchild-unreachable
dispatch/syscall-exec.c:64     # auto-disable 32-bit syscalls path inside do_syscall(); child_process() dispatch; no fork() between here and the lock acquire
dispatch/syscall-post.c:160    # deactivate_enosys(): post-exec ENOSYS deactivation; child_process() dispatch path only; grandchild-unreachable
child/child-periodic.c:61      # check_parent_pid(): buglock acquired to write reparent BUG message; child periodic handler called from child_process() maintenance loop; no fork() on path
